    "The proposed development, by virtue lack of sufficient information and justification regarding the potential loss of historic fabric, would result in 'less than substantial' harm to the special architectural and historic interest of the listed building as a designated heritage asset, which is not outweighed by any public benefits. The proposal is therefore contrary to Sections 16(2), 66 (1) and 72 (1) of the Planning (Listed Building and Conservation Areas) Act 1990, 12 and 16 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2021), Policies D5, HC1 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 and CP31 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD11, DMD37 and DMD44 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), the Enfield Town Conservation Area Management proposals (2015), and the Enfield Heritage Strategy 2019 - 2024 (2019)."
